+
+## 8m. 2026-10-24: the cut, named (decision D2 of the axiom audit)
+
+The continuity auditor found that the language had no word for a change that takes no time: `morph … 0s` worked
+but was undocumented, the README called morph "the only way anything moves", so Claude never wrote it (0 of 220
+morphs in 63 real turns), and the electron of a quantum-jump scene slid through n = 2 while the voice said "never
+in between" (frame at 3.7 s, cue at 3.18 s). An uncued `0s` passed `--check` clean and the history said only
+"done".
+
+**Decided:** the cut is `0s` on a morph (no new verb or key: a cut is a morph of no duration, the end of the
+`0.05s` continuum). It is drawn as an event, an afterimage: the thing as it was fades where it was over 0.6 s
+(a trail of zero length, so it has a trail's meaning and no other; the new place needs no flash, an abrupt onset
+captures the eye on its own). The history names it (`# since: morph e.level 1 -> 3 0s done`). A cut with no cue
+word is linted (`continuity:`) and counts as an axiom warning in `--check`. Rejected: a `cut` verb (two spellings
+of one thing, nothing to read back), `ease=step` (a wait plus a cut), a `discrete=` flag on the thing, fade-out
+then fade-in (two things, three lines).
+
+**Built:** engine (`Afterimage`, `leaveAfterimage`, `afterimage(id)`, the lint in `analyze`, the log suffix),
+render (`drawAfterimages` under the shapes, names off the trace), `main.cpp` (the axiom count), README (the morph
+line, a Modifiers bullet, the dictionary row, axiom 4's stated exception), prompt (a "Show what you say" row and a
+pitfall), toolbox ("A change that takes no time (a cut)"). Test: an uncued cut is linted and the readback says
+`0s`; a cued one is clean; live, the afterimage of a `0s` morph is > 0.3 one frame in and gone 0.75 s later, and an
+eased morph leaves none (3 of 8 assertions fail on the old engine). Regressions: test 192/192, check 93 scenes +
+32 moves ok, golden 52/52 same on both placers, append 152 identical + the 4 known 3D cases. Frames: the electron
+jumps on the word with a dimmer dot fading on n = 1; the treaty's old border and ceded strip fade; the price gap's
+trail keeps its true gap.
+
+**Not done:** no afterimage for text, blocks, boxes, notes, params or 3D things (a param's dependents jump without
+a trace); the afterimage is not in `picture()` (like pulses); no corpus measurement of how often Claude now
+writes a cut, and whether it over-uses it (the prompt says rare).
